# An ask: a wanderer who's been bitten. The antidote is always given, never taken (the built
# "Give them your antidote"). Mercy, not jokes.

conv wanderer.bitten.arm
for wanderer
when wbitten
topic "Let me see that arm."
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say Don't. I know what it is. I've seen enough of them on the road to know the shape of it, and how long it gives you.
  say There's a house with a bear on the door near enough, if I walk fast. They'd sit with me there. Or there's nothing. I'm still deciding which.
  > @give Here. Take my antidote. -> given   do call:slot:2
  > @house Get to a house and tell them. Now. -> house
  > @sit I'll sit with you a minute. -> sit

node given
  say You'd give me that. To me. You don't even know my name. I don't know what to say. I'll take it before you change your mind, and I'll owe you for as long as I've got.
  > @back1 You owe me nothing. One more thing. -> hub

node house
  say They'll help if they can. That's the rule at every house with the bear on the door: say it out loud, and they help. I'll go now, while my legs still work.
  > @back2 Go on, then. One more thing first. -> hub

node sit
  say Thank you. Nobody's sat with me since the roads closed. Don't talk about the arm. Tell me something ordinary. Anything at all.
  > @weather The weather's turning. Rain tonight. -> weather

node weather
  say Is it. Good. I always liked rain on a roof. That's what I wanted. Something that'll still be happening tomorrow, whatever happens to me.
  > @back3 It will be. Let me ask you something. -> hub
